## Change

Only `/app/fixture/lib/index.mjs` was modified (`git status`: just that file; `package.json`, `cordis.patch.yml`, README untouched):

- `inject`: `['tasks', 'httpServer']` → `['jobs', 'webServer']`
- `ctx.tasks` → `ctx.jobs`, `ctx.httpServer.register` → `ctx.webServer.register`
- `tasks.onTaskDone` → `jobs.onJobDone`
- Route shape, `/bench-status/status` path, and `{"ok":true,"open":N}` payload left byte-identical
- The stale header comment (which claimed the old names were correct and told readers not to rename) was corrected to describe the post-0812 contract, with no retired identifiers left in the file

## Host contract check (dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2)

- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-webserver`: `ctx.webServer`, `register({ kind, path, handler })` — same shape as before
- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-jobs`: `ctx.jobs.list(caller?)`, `ctx.jobs.onJobDone((snapshot, owner) => …)`
- `--dump-config` shows the `webserver` and `jobs` entries in the composed web tree

## Verification (isolated `DSH_HOME` profiles under `/app`, since the sandbox blocks `/root/.dsh`)

- **Before the rename** (original file): cold boot failed exactly as stated — `@demo/dsh-bench-status: pending (waiting for services: tasks, httpServer)` → `plugin tree failed to load`.
- **After the rename**, installed fresh via `dsh plugin --profile web add /app/fixture`: boot reached `dsh web: http://127.0.0.1:3080/?token=<redacted> with `0` pending entries and `0` failed entries.
- **Route smoke test**: `GET /bench-status/status` → `200` with body `{"ok":true,"open":0}`; an unregistered sibling path → `404`. The `onJobDone` registration also succeeded (a missing method would have failed activation).

One environmental caveat, unrelated to the fixture: after printing the `dsh web:` URL, a stock web profile in this container exits on `user patch-layer watching requires the Cordis HMR service` — the installed `cordis-plugin-hmr@1.0.19` lacks the `registerConfig` API that `dsh-app-boot` expects for live patch watching. I confirmed the identical crash with **no fixture installed**, so it is host-side. For the stable HTTP smoke test I set `patchReload: "startup"` in the disposable verification profile only; the standard flow still reaches `dsh web:` with no pending entry, which is the migration's success signal. All scratch profiles and stores were cleaned up afterwards.

